WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
In 1517, Martin Luther,
a friar at Wittenberg,

2
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.750
attacked the sale of
indulgences in 95 Theses.

3
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.300
The quarrel over indulgences became
a quarrel over justification:

4
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:16.600
how is a sinner made righteous before God?

5
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.500
His answer rested on verses like this one:

6
00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.260
the righteous shall live by faith.

7
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.030
But if God accepts you
before you do anything good,

8
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.390
why bother being good at all?

9
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:30.500
In this mission, you'll read
the verses Luther built on,

10
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.460
from Romans, Ephesians and Galatians.

11
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.990
Then you'll see why Christians
have disagreed about how:

12
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.530
by faith alone, by faith and
works, or by God's choice.

13
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:45.710
Your mission: find out how Luther
and Calvin answered that question.
